# Next.js & TypeScript Standards

## Next.js 15 App Router Standards

### File Structure
- Use App Router structure in `app/` directory
- Page components in `app/[route]/page.tsx`
- Layout components in `app/layout.tsx`
- Global styles in `app/globals.css`

### Component Standards
- Use TypeScript for all components
- Export default for page components
- Use proper TypeScript interfaces for props
- Implement proper error boundaries

### Import Standards
```tsx
// 1. Next.js imports
import Link from "next/link";
import Image from "next/image";

// 2. React imports
import { useState, useEffect } from "react";

// 3. Custom components
import { SoundBoard } from "@/components/SoundBoard";
import { EmptyState } from "@/components/EmptyState";

// 4. Icons
import { PlayIcon } from "@heroicons/react/24/outline";

// 5. Utilities
import { cn } from "@/utils/helpers";
```

### Metadata Standards
Always include proper metadata in layout.tsx:
```tsx
export const metadata: Metadata = {
  title: "Page Title - TuneSlap",
  description: "SEO-optimized description",
  keywords: "relevant, keywords, here",
  openGraph: {
    title: "Page Title - TuneSlap",
    description: "SEO-optimized description",
    type: "website",
  },
};
```

## TypeScript Standards

### Type Definitions
- Use proper TypeScript interfaces
- Avoid `any` types
- Use strict type checking
- Define props interfaces for components

### Component Props
```tsx
interface ComponentProps {
  title: string;
  description?: string;
  children?: React.ReactNode;
}

export function Component({ title, description, children }: ComponentProps) {
  // Component implementation
}
```

## Performance Standards

### Image Optimization
- Always use Next.js Image component
- Include proper alt text
- Use appropriate sizes and priority flags
- Optimize for different screen sizes

### Code Splitting
- Use dynamic imports for heavy components
- Implement proper loading states
- Use Suspense boundaries where appropriate

### SEO Optimization
- Use semantic HTML elements
- Include proper heading hierarchy (h1, h2, h3)
- Add meta descriptions and keywords
- Implement structured data where relevant

## Accessibility Standards
- Use semantic HTML elements
- Include proper ARIA labels
- Ensure keyboard navigation works
- Maintain proper color contrast ratios
- Use descriptive alt text for images
